/-!
# A finite partition for representative certificates

The two masks select candidate placement and longer-product branches; all
other candidates use the short-element branch. These definitions make no
membership, order, or coverage assertion. Cases on the selector are exhaustive
regardless of whether the exploratory labels are correct. Each branch needs
its own complete proof for the actual literal representatives.

Source: original untrusted enumeration of Parrott's p.683 generators, in
`RepresentativeWitnesses/source/`. Products and conjugates act on the left.
-/

@[expose] public section
namespace Tits.MinimumIndex.LargeTwoOvergroups.SeedOvergroups.ExtensionObstructions.RepresentativeCertificates

/-- The three independently certifiable branches of the finite calculation. -/
inductive WitnessCase where
  | short | place | product
  deriving DecidableEq

